    "title": "Can I see Artemis II launch from Jersey Shore? Visibility map, updates",
    "text": "NEWSWhen is Artemis II launch time? Can you watch launch at Jersey Shore? Lori ComstockUSA TODAY NETWORKApril 1, 2026, 3:46 p.m. ETNASA's Artemis II launch countdown is on as the Artemis II crew gets ready to launch from Florida's Kennedy Space Center in Cape Canaveral as soon as 6:24 p.m. ET tonight in a historic rocket launch that has an eastern launch path that could be visible in New Jersey, particularly along the Jersey Shore.The astronauts on Artemis 2 — NASA astronauts Reid Wiseman, Christina Koch and Victor Glover and Canadian astronaut Jeremy Hansen — won't land on the moon but will be the first humans to launch toward the moon since the Apollo 17 mission in 1972, more than 50 years ago.Our editors independently choose our recommendations. Some content is produced with paid support from a third party, however our editorial decisions remain independent. If you buy through our links, the USA TODAY Network may earn a commission. Prices and availability may change.",
